title HUNK21 — the Photos app tunes saturation
prompt baton prin recur — continue the loop past HUNK20, next agent-doable Lindy-first crux, send each increment
think REMEMBER named the next crux: another Photos gesture (a smoother resampler, or hue/saturation as a bounded verb). Lindy-first crux-first favors saturation — a capability every photo app carries, and unlike a floating-point HSL round-trip it admits a clean integer-only, algebra-provable shape over the open module already built.
think Chose the luma-preserving map out = L + (c-L)*num/den, clamped, with Rec.601 weights scaled to sum exactly 256 (77+150+29) so gray maps to itself with no drift. num==den recovers the source, num==0 flattens to a true grayscale, a gray pixel is a fixed point, i64 keeps every product from wrapping, saturate_max bounds the term.
think Proved by algebra not one arithmetic: neutral byte-identical, zero-saturation r==g==b==luma per pixel, already-gray fixed point at every saturation, a boost drives the dominant channel above and the weak channel below its luma, alpha pass-through, purity, still-open round-trip, and the named refusals (BadSaturation, EmptyImage).
obs Built GREEN first try; all five photos selftests GREEN (crop, orient, scale, adjust, saturate). Added a small luma_of helper (its own two invariants, the weight-sum assert) that a future hue rotation will reuse.
obs A true hue rotation — modular color-wheel turn, cleanest as a luma-chroma matrix — is genuinely harder to bound cleanly in integer math; named as a horizon on the same module rather than half-built here.
obs TAME bans clean, width exit 0; no new compound asserts.
